{:edb/db-before-t 1379 :edb/db-after-t 1380 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534692 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:19:09.093Z" 13194139534692 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303697 13194139534692 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303704 13194139534692 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303690 13194139534692 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303711 13194139534692 true] [17592186096726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303683 13194139534692 true] [17592186303683 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303684 13194139534692 true] [17592186303683 1089 "q-104813" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303683 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534692 true] [17592186303683 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039683/assets/931802565a13dac284496f41ebb19238402056689a96288b2fbb1dd9f018ae12.png)\n\nGiven the plots of $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ above, find ${h}^{′}(-1)$ where $h(x)=\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.$" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303683 1113 #uuid "d55ca840-bf7c-5f00-aa1e-3953e088e6a0" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303683 1145 "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(-1)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)\\cdot g(-1)-f(-1)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph above, we obtain that $f(-1)=0$ and $g(-1)=1.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,2)$ equals $\\frac{2}{3}.$ So, ${f}^{′}(-1)=\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-3,2)$ equals $1.$ So, ${g}^{′}(-1)=1.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(-1) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)\\cdot g(-1)-f(-1)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303685 13194139534692 true] [17592186303684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303686 13194139534692 true] [17592186303684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303687 1319