2253e-1bb5-55a8-8d37-5f1d7c2b6670" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303690 1145 "The product rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)={f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)+f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(-3)={f}^{′}(-3)\\cdot g(-3)+f(-3)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-3).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(-3)=-2$ and $g(-3)=0.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,2)$ equals $1.$ So, ${f}^{′}(-3)=1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,-2)$ equals $3.$ So, ${g}^{′}(-3)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(-3) & ={f}^{′}(-3)\\cdot g(-3)+f(-3)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303692 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303693 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303694 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303695 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303696 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1041 "selection" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303696 13194139534692 true] [17592186303691 1110 #uuid "3c2ec269-4e2c-53e0-baf3-eab83225eae9" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303692 1034 "3" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303692 1111 #uuid "f92ca9e4-bd3b-5fdb-93e6-2b2cbd38e187" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303693 1034 "6" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303693 1111 #uuid "cd9a0ee1-7f2c-5c94-b546-d4f0cf99e6cc" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303694 1034 "-3" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303694 1111 #uuid "e91ad000-9ac3-555a-93cc-1cc4c8e5b952" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303695 1034 "0" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303695 1111 #uuid "1e2236d3-d2c6-5cd2-8740-166622627c98" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303696 1034 "-6" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303696 1111 #uuid "7598c2f7-07f6-5518-85a7-2b621e8fa58a" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303697 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303698 13194139534692 true] [17592186303697 1089 "q-15659" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303697 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534692 true] [17592186303697 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039683/assets/cf3cc180e5489aa83c17b47db641aae68d03b095085102a29a2942a783369c07.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find ${h}^{′}(3)$ where $h(x)=f(x)+g(x).$" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303697 1113 #uuid "4862b6d5-1eb7-573f-b085-daa585633ca3" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303697 1145 "The addition rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)={f}^{′}(x)+{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(3)={f}^{′}(3)+{g}^{′}(3).\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that $x=3$ corresponds to\n\n- the interval $x\\in (2,4)$ for the function $f,$ and\n\n- the interval $x\\in (2.5,4)$ for the function $g,$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039683/assets/19a32fa6a7b2b6481052ab3539838bb00d486f92ea3f08b54efa2a1cfc69d221.png)\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (2,4)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=\\frac{0-2}{4-2}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(3)=-1.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (2.5,4)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δg}{Δx}=\\frac{1-1}{4-2.5}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${g}^{′}(3)=0.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(3) & ={f}^{′}(3)+{g}^{′}(3) \\\\  & =-1+0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303699 13194139534692 true] [17592186303698 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303700 13194139534692 true] [175921