704 1113 #uuid "cf012889-ec8e-5d4a-9556-68a3d9dfb3d0" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303704 1145 "The addition and constant multiple rules for derivatives give\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)={f}^{′}(x)-{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(2)={f}^{′}(2)-{g}^{′}(2).\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that $x=2$ corresponds to \n\n- the interval $x\\in (-2,3)$ for the function $f,$ and\n\n- the interval $x\\in (-2,3)$ for the function $g,$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039683/assets/299b996bf08e4b4e8560d013829ddd1f42751767cd3f00dcd04c23c95f2c62b4.png)\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (-2,3)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=\\frac{1-1}{3-(-2)}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (-2,3)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δg}{Δx}=\\frac{3-(-2)}{3-(-2)}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${g}^{′}(2)=1.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & ={f}^{′}(2)-{g}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =0-1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303706 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303707 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303708 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303709 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303710 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1041 "selection" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303709 13194139534692 true] [17592186303705 1110 #uuid "6c8a970e-9196-5bfe-871a-28900d6b1880" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303706 1034 "3" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303706 1111 #uuid "0eef874d-155f-5e06-b4c9-f3d9b856bf53" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303707 1034 "2" 13194139534692 true] [17592186303707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534692 true] [17592186303707 1111 #